  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nThis PR adds stage 3 of the path kernel (K3): the load control stage. The stage changes guide curves only. It adds no entry, no link and no lift. No old planner changes. With the default switch, the output is identical.\n\n## Public surface (`camcraft_pathkernel::load`)\n\n- `LoadStage` implements `LoadPlanner`. `LoadStage::new(limit)` sets the limit (ae/D) that the stage uses for `None` and `Trochoidal`, which have no limit of their own. `Default` is 0.5 (a 90 degree contact).\n- `LoadControl::None`: the set does not change. Each read above `limit x (1 + PLAN_TOL)` gets an `OverLimit` record (`NO_CONTROL`). The verdict has one status line `Note` for each reason, with the count, the worst load and its place.\n- `LoadControl::ConstantEngagement` with `Reach::Rings`: the stage inserts a mid-level ring where a ring reads above the load. An insertion that does not lower the load is removed, and the cut gets a name (`NOT_FIXED`, the sharp corner of offset rings). The other names are `FRESH_CUT`, `NOT_A_RING`, `AT_FLOOR` and `TOO_MANY_PASSES`.\n- `Reach::Stock` (Adaptive) is refused with `STOCK_REACH_ELSEWHERE`. The HSM planner stays behind the load trait (K0 record, revision 2).\n- `LoadControl::Trochoidal`: each `FullWidth` stretch becomes loops that walk the stretch. The free room sets the loop size. If no loop fits, the stretch stays and gets a name. The names are `NO_ROOM`, `LOOPS_OVER` and `NOT_MARKED`. A loop point outside the area is refused (`LOOP_LEAVES`).\n- One engagement law for all modes (`load/law.rs`). The stage makes a raster of the `StockRead` stock and reads it in the cut order: ae/D = (1 - cos phi) / 2 at the rim of the swept disc. `NO_RASTER` refuses a region that has no raster.\n- A `FullWidth` mark that has no read above the limit is resolved and removed. A mark that stays is named by its reads. `Controlled::new` stays the single gate for law 6.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `camcraft-pathkernel` `laws`, new `load_stage.rs`: the stage runs with the kit, the ring planner (K2), `OrderStage` and `LinkStage` (K4). The fixtures are the disc pocket, the pocket with an island, and two lobes with a neck (a `FullWidth` mark).\n  - `k3_none_keeps_the_curves_and_names_every_cut_above_the_limit`\n  - `k3_constant_engagement_leaves_no_unnamed_cut_above_the_limit`\n  - `k3_trochoidal_leaves_no_full_width_feed_in_the_marked_stretch`\n  - `k3_a_stretch_with_no_room_for_a_loop_stays_and_is_named`\n  - `k3_an_unnamed_cut_above_the_limit_and_a_bad_limit_are_refused`: an unnamed over-limit read; a limit that is NaN, -0.1, 0 or 1.5; the stock reach; a tool radius that is not a number.\n- `camcraft-motion` `kernel_laws`, new `k3_load.rs`: `kernel_load_control_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone`. It uses the law measures of #4154 at a 25 % load. `k4_order_link.rs` gets `kernel_path_with`, which puts a load stage between order and link. The K4 pin does not change.\n\n## Readings (measured, no constant tuned)\n\nLaw suite (the check grid of the suite; hot = a read above `load x 1.05`):\n\n| Fixture (load) | Kernel, None: curves / hot reads / worst ae/D | Kernel, constant engagement: curves / hot reads (unnamed) / worst ae/D |\n|---|---|---|\n| disc pocket (0.25) | 4 / 3 / 0.413 | 9 / 0 (0) / 0.179 |\n| pocket with an island (0.20) | 12 / 286 / 0.999 | 29 / 146 (0) / 0.998 |\n| two lobes and a neck (0.40) | 9 / 249 / 0.998 | 27 / 128 (0) / 0.998 |\n\nTrochoidal on the neck: the worst read in the marked stretch is 0.941. Before, it was 1.0 (full width). All loops stay in the cutter-centre area.\n\nMotion `kernel_laws` (#4154 meter, limit 60 degrees, the band round the part). Each cell gives the feed moves above the limit, the worst angle in degrees, and the moves above the limit with no named place within one tool radius:\n\n| Case | Old 2D Pocket | Kernel without load control (None) | Kernel with constant engagement |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| disc Inside | 20 / 178 / all | 3507 / 173 / 0 | 833 / 173 / 1 |\n| disc Outside | 20 / 178 / all | 402 / 145 / 13 | 334 / 118 / 74 |\n| dog bone Inside | 32 / 180 / all | 2587 / 173 / 0 | 581 / 173 / 1 |\n| dog bone Outside | 32 / 180 / all | 724 / 167 / 3 | 678 / 143 / 66 |\n\n- The kernel counts each short move of its dense rings. Thus its counts and the old counts do not compare one to one. The first K4 reading was over 3504 on the disc Inside. It is 3507 on this base.\n- The worst value Inside (173 degrees) is the first ring round the part. It is a full-width cut with no pass beside it, and it is named (`FRESH_CUT`).\n- The unnamed moves on the Outside rows are on the stock edge line, where a piece starts after a lift. There the kernel read and the #4154 meter differ. Follow-up: #4260 (P7). The one unnamed move on each Inside row is a link feed (stage 5).\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/4026-kernel-load-control.md`. In short:\n- The stage has a limit of its own for `None` and `Trochoidal`.\n- Constant engagement inserts passes. It does not make a new spiral or a new ladder.\n- The stock reach is refused by name.\n- The trochoid walks the stretch, and the free room sets its size.\n- The reader reads after the clear, outside the edge. The first form read inside the edge and gave values that were too low (54 degrees where the geometry gives 64).\n\n## Gates on the final head\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p camcraft-pathkernel` and `-p camcraft-motion`: pass.\n- `camcraft-pathkernel --test laws`: 130 passed.\n- `camcraft-motion --test kernel_laws`: 30 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-pathkernel --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `-p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: 4 steps, all ok (pathkernel lib, pathkernel laws, motion kernel_laws).\n- `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work` of camcraft-app: 43 passed (4 ignored), 1 passed, 1 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 7 steps, all ok (motion light lib and `adaptive_troch_island`, `_neck`, `_parallel`; app light `pocket_pass_start`, `offset_pass_start`).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No kind plans on the kernel yet. The registry table does not change. Each K6 group moves its kinds.\n- Constant engagement with the stock reach (Adaptive): refused by this stage.\n- Trochoidal on a fixture of #3932 with an open edge and a near wall. The loops walk the marked stretch, but no pin uses that fixture.\n- The #3849 law is covered by construction: each curve is read, and the clean-up rings too (`each_curve_read`). There is no clean-up fixture of #1587.\n- The loop sense from climb or conventional. A microlift return between loops (stage 5).\n- The tool shapes that are not a disc. The lathe plane.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #4026\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
